==Early entrants==
===College underclassmen===
Following last year's slight dip of underclassmen, entering the new millennium, this draft saw a total of 55 underclassmen declare for the NBA draft initially. However, for collegiate players, seven of the nineteen total players that ultimately withdrew their names would be collegiate players (with Joshua Cross from [[Southern Illinois Salukis men's basketball|Southern Illinois University]], [[Jason Kapono]] from [[UCLA Bruins men's basketball|UCLA]], [[Brian Merriweather]] from the [[UT Rio Grande Valley Vaqueros men's basketball|University of Texas Pan-American]], [[Jeryl Sasser]] from [[SMU Mustangs men's basketball|Southern Methodist University]], [[Kenny Satterfield]] from the [[Cincinnati Bearcats men's basketball|University of Cincinnati]], [[Karim Shabazz]] from [[Providence Friars men's basketball|Providence College]], and Joe White from [[Texas A&M Aggies men's basketball|Texas A&M University]] being the collegiate players that withdrew their names). Overall, including the high schools and international players with the 26 college underclassmen, there were 36 total players that would be considered underclassmen. That being said, the following [[college basketball]] players successfully applied for early draft entrance.<ref name=tdr>{{cite web |title=2000 Underclassmen |url=https://www.thedraftreview.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=3047:2000-underclassmen&catid=136&Itemid=384 |website=The Draft Review | date=August 4, 2007 |access-date=December 21, 2022}}</ref>

